{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon","id":1376848,"title":"A lost pantheon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-27T13:13:08-07:00","id":1376848,"title":"A lost pantheon?","content":"Try this idea...<br /> <br /> When mount Tambora blew up in the early 19th century and caused the &quot;Year without a Summer&quot; the peoples of the island we're almost entirely wiped out. A large and to all reports fairly advanced culture lived on the less visited side of the island. They were truly obliterated. Not only do we not have even one word of their language ( although we know other Islanders said it was different than any other language they knew, and these people understood about languages being related) we don't even know what they called themselves. Hey, we don't really even know what they were called.<br /> <br /> Now try this idea. A few members of the pantheon of these people have gotten over their depression and come back to the world.<br /> <br /> Basically, how would you handle a lost Pantheon. All of their myths are gone. Their language is not just extinct, it's totally lost. So they can be built from the ground up. Giving the Storyteller free reign. <br /> <br /> Would other pantheons seek to recruit them. Shun them? Drive them off?<br /> <br /> Could they build a new place in the world? Maybe taking over pop culture myths and molding them into something worthwhile.<br /> <br /> What do you think. Given the place they lived, their gods could fit several different patterns. They were known to be sophisticated and in a multicultural area of the Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T13:21:34-07:00","id":1376849,"title":"","content":"This is a rather interesting idea. Unknown Orphan gods you say... hmmm that sounds like potential incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T14:42:43-07:00","id":1376998,"title":"","content":"I would be exceptionally careful doing something like this. These were real people who existed, with their own culture and values and traditions that, as you say, we know nothing about. Should we be using this dead culture as a coat-hanger to build a fictional religion off of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T15:12:08-07:00","id":1377000,"title":"","content":"We already do. And the dead culture was destroyed by a volcano that wiped them completely out. There are no known descendents nor any way to trace descendents. As I said, it's not just we don't know what they called themselves, we have no idea what their neighbors called them. The closest we get to non archeological data is the testimony of one old Indonesian woman (and as she must have lived and died under Dutch rule that description is limited) who said her father told her they were impressive (her words, she was fluent in English, as well as Dutch and French) she also said, &quot;I think you English and the Dutch would have said they were advanced.&quot; What she based her opinions on, other than her father's word, I don't know.<br /> <br /> As these folks are a total blank beyond the archeology saying they had large numbers of horses and excellent metalwork. And oh yes, they existed. <br /> <br /> Read the book Ireland's Immortals. You'll see most of what we think we know of the Irish Pantheon is mainly fiction. Heck, we keep on finding out that most of what we say we know about the Olympians is really Renaissance Italian fiction about the Greek gods.<br /> <br /> I can't see the harm. Especially when no one can be hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T15:29:31-07:00","id":1377002,"title":"","content":"Dude, are you aware who it is you just asked to research Irish mythology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:12:30-07:00","id":1377007,"title":"","content":"No. I hope he's Irish if you're so shocked. But we really know far less than we think we do about the Irish deites.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm of Irish descent and have an Irish surname. I've read what been available to me (pathetically little) about Irish culture and history. So don't dismiss me lightly, use solid facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-28-2020, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T16:34:03-07:00","id":1377012,"title":"","content":"Watcher is a PHD candidate in Celtic Studies, with a focus on mythology. He may even have the degree by now for all I know. He's an actual, honest-to-goodness, expert, and a hardcore academic in regards to this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T17:45:16-07:00","id":1377025,"title":"","content":"Good to know. I wish I had the knack for languages. Still, my point is sound. We routinely create fictions out of other people's cultures. As an American, I'm routinely made into a subhuman monster in the fictions of more than a hundred nations. anti-Americanism is a fashionable and accepted bigotry. The people wiped out by Tambora are beyond all pain. If I create a fiction based on them they can feel no harm. Meanwhile flesh and blood Americans pay for the lies told about America. But no one would ever restrain themselves from making harmful and slandering fictions about America because of that. <br /> <br /> Myself, I intend neither lies or slander. So I bitterly resent being scolded. Watcher assumed a position of moral superiority and told me to conform for no justifiable reason. I think I was polite in response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-28-2020, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T18:12:39-07:00","id":1377031,"title":"","content":"I mean if I wanted to just come up with a fictional mythology in Scion I'd probably pick a 'lost' culture I just fucking made up whole cloth. Can't get anything wrong about an ancient culture if I completely invented them.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Watcher's comment felt more to me like advising of caution rather than moralizing. Just going &quot;Careful there, remember these were a real people&quot; isn't really scolding, anymore than going &quot;Hey if you take this turn at 45 mph your car may flip&quot; is scolding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-28-2020, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T19:00:00-07:00","id":1377040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377031#post1377031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if I wanted to just come up with a fictional mythology in Scion I'd probably pick a 'lost' culture I just fucking made up whole cloth. Can't get anything wrong about an ancient culture if I completely invented them.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Watcher's comment felt more to me like advising of caution rather than moralizing. Just going &quot;Careful there, remember these were a real people&quot; isn't really scolding, anymore than going &quot;Hey if you take this turn at 45 mph your car may flip&quot; is scolding.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be right, but I saw a perfect historical blank. If a put a pantheon in many other places, there is someone living there. The other side of Tambora is a perfect blank. Anything can be put there without consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T19:33:14-07:00","id":1377044,"title":"","content":"I would say the Scion has already done something like that, with the Gaelic Pantheon (Nemontedavos, I think?). This just takes it to an extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T19:57:51-07:00","id":1377048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377012#post1377012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watcher is a PHD candidate in Celtic Studies, with a focus on mythology. He may even have the degree by now for all I know. He's an actual, honest-to-goodness, expert, and a hardcore academic in regards to this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might want to tone it down to, I'm sure Watcher appreciate the validity of what Astromancer said. Academics are also people that can be interacted with in a manner beyond just only asking questions, you can have conversations with them, they aren't living mangods.<br /> <br /> Astromancer seems to see the concern, but this is an alternate reality how is this more disrespectful then say Vampire saying Pampei was destroyed to wipe out demons, or that Carthage literally supported and worshipped Demonic Demigods. Or that Sri Lanka was literally ruled by Demon King Ravana in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T20:56:02-07:00","id":1377056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377000#post1377000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the book Ireland's Immortals. You'll see most of what we think we know of the Irish Pantheon is mainly fiction. Heck, we keep on finding out that most of what we say we know about the Olympians is really Renaissance Italian fiction about the Greek gods.<br /> <br /> I can't see the harm. Especially when no one can be hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have read the book, it is quite good! There are some parts I disagree with, but those are mostly just pedantic side issues I have with the Fomorian stuff in it. That's just my own personal theories involved there though rather than anything against the work as a whole. Mark is a great guy, absolute sweetheart. He's been the mentor of one of my best friends when he was still working at Cambridge and I really look forward to getting to meet him in person. His writing has had a big effect on me.<br /> <br /> I have honestly spent more than time than I probably ought to have thinking about the nature of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 as effectively a... retroactively constructed pagan past in the specific context of Scion. I'll not bore people with it, but if it is a topic that interests you and you like Mark's book, I have it all written up in one of the PDFs in my signature.<br /> <br /> As people have said, I wasn't saying it <i>shouldn't</i> be done, I was just saying it is something that it would probably be a good idea to take some caution with. You know, just like The Lorax said, 'I Speak for the Trees, for the Trees have no tongues.' My mantra is that I Speak for the Dead, for the Dead have no tongues. While we might not hurt anyone by misrepresenting and mistreating them, you know, what can we do but aspire to kindness? If you want to do something with them, maybe base it off those final interviews and the archaeological findings? Even though nobody can be 'hurt,' doing that little bit of extra legwork to do these forgotten people a kindness is just a nice thing. As you yourself point out, you have been hurt by negative depictions of America in pop culture and media at large, evidently you can see how this sort of lack of care can hurt people. While there not be any members of this culture left, you can give their memory the respect you would want your own culture to receive, that sorta thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you are interested in more material to learn about Irish sagas, just drop me a line! I am more than happy to share whatever I can and give suggestions to help people learn about medieval Irish literature!<br /> <br /> (Also, I go by they, but, no big deal)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just because I don't come on here a lot, also, the Nemetondevos are going to be the like... 'Gaulish' Pantheon, but I expect it'll be more like the 'Classical Era Celts' as the Gauls cut out all of Britain, Celtiberia, the Anatolian Celts, the Central European Celts, a lotta people. Gaelic is a language term for... oh boy, let's see if I can get this from memory. Languages descended from Miiiidle Irish? I think? It is based on a medieval ethnonym for the Irish.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT 2: I really hate double posting so I'm just adding stuff in edits. Yeah, I'm just a random human being. Me being an academic just means I've made bad life choices and now know quite honestly far too much about really niche topics. I'm totally capable of being wrong. I've been wrong in the past, and I'm going to be wrong again, its a great habit of mine. I just happen to have more tools on hand to make a fool of myself and the ability to do it in such niche topics I'll probably not be corrected on it until I've been dead for twenty years when the next person bothers to care about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 03-29-2020, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T21:13:01-07:00","id":1377059,"title":"","content":"I am not personally comfortable with the idea of inventing my own OCs and declaring them to be part of a real-world culture or religion without significant precautions being taken. I personally have no interest in making my own gods, but, should you desire to do so, I think Kyman has the perfect solution: create your own original culture. Atlantis, after all, can be more or less whatever you want it to be, and there are countless mythological cultures the world over should you desire to do so. Hell, I could even see some of the races of Denizens (or at least the ones that don't serve specific deities already) having their own religions and pantheons.<br /> <br /> As for the Nemetendevos, Zemis, Aisar, Alihah, and so on and so forth, there is a big difference between pantheons where information is scarce and pantheons where information is nonexistent. I think Watcher and Sacerdos's take on the Zemis is a great model for how to handle such a pantheon and deal with the presence of unknowns in the narrative. While some liberties of course had to be taken, everything has SOME basis in the lore. None of the individual deities were completely invented. That's different than making up a religion and declaring that it belonged to a real-world culture group, which is what would presumably have to happen here.<br /> <br /> The comparison with Vampire is a bit of a false equivalency. Vampire is not a mythology adaptation and presents no illusions of being one. It has some mythological inspiration, as does most urban fantasy, but that's different than something which attempts to adapt real-world religions in their entirety into its lore.<br /> <br /> Also, in Scion, the Deva write-up made it very clear that the Lanka which Ravana rules over is a Terra Incognita and not the same as the real world Sri Lanka. For all we know, the local Sinhalese deities could eventually be adapted, and certainly not as slaves or minions of Ravana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 03-29-2020, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:07:23-07:00","id":1377076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377048#post1377048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astromancer seems to see the concern, but this is an alternate reality how is this more disrespectful then say Vampire saying Pampei was destroyed to wipe out demons, or that Carthage literally supported and worshipped Demonic Demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtM is hardly the best example to give of a game that treats all cultures respectfully, given the justified criticism it has received for it's portrayal of several of them *cough* Ravnos *cough* The question was never 'How is this more disrespectful' but 'why can't it be more respectful'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377048#post1377048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that Sri Lanka was literally ruled by Demon King Ravana in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the thing Scion 2e explicitly says is *not* the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:45:42-07:00","id":1377097,"title":"","content":"Given that this is a game, I think avoiding disrespect is good enough. You can go overboard on being respectful, to the point that it starts interfering with the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T23:32:13-07:00","id":1377107,"title":"","content":"If the borders of respect are drawn based on whether a culture is still alive to feel offended by it, how much respect is that really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T23:38:02-07:00","id":1377108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377097#post1377097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that this is a game, I think avoiding disrespect is good enough. You can go overboard on being respectful, to the point that it starts interfering with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert on, well, anything, but I can at least try to use the bare minimum of respect. And I don't think that in any way interferes with running a game or playing in one.<br /> <br /> I mean I'll agree that getting too focused on the details and worrying about the smallest details may not be productive to every game group, but y'know... We can TRY for basic decency.<br /> <br /> Like, the original idea... At its core, it's going &quot;We know this culture existed but very little else so why not just make up a Pantheon?&quot; and my problem with that is... If you're going to make things up completely? To the point where you have no idea if there's even any tenuous connective tissue? <i>Why bother tying them to that culture</i>?<br /> <br /> Like, if you have information here and there, but have to use conjecture and supposition to fill in some blanks, then sure. But if all we have is a name of a God (and they may not even be a God because we don't have any additional context) so you're making up who they are, what they did, what their practices were, what relationships they have with other Possible Gods (half of whom you made up because we don't even have THOSE names in any records)... Like, if you're making up 99% of a Pantheon, you might as well just commit to your own original creation. I'm sure the original Gods that are being made up are absolutely fine, and heck, may even be great fun to read about.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to slap Alejandro the Savior, my original character, into the Teotl as a God and insist that he was worshipped in the mid 1200s by the Aztec people*. Because they <i>probably</i> didn't. Yes, it's my table, and yes, it's my history of my World, but... Kali, Krishna, and Christ, I can fucking <i>try</i> to treat this with a modicum of respect. And in my mind, part of that Respect is &quot;Stick to what I know is Important, find out if I don't know what's important&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, what Manus noted. It's kind of like claiming &quot;Well it doesn't matter if I insult Jim when he's not in the room&quot;.<br /> <br /> *Now if I'm doing something mad like, my players have agreed to a Historical Eras game and one of the PCs achieved Apotheosis in the early 13th century then sure I'll acknowledge them if a game takes place further down in the same timeline but by THIS point we've careened off into Full Historical AU Fanfiction<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T23:42:47-07:00","id":1377110,"title":"","content":"We don't have the names of any gods by the way, we don't even know if they were polytheistic at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T00:05:57-07:00","id":1377112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377108#post1377108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not an expert on, well, anything, but I can at least try to use the bare minimum of respect. And I don't think that in any way interferes with running a game or playing in one.<br /> <br /> I mean I'll agree that getting too focused on the details and worrying about the smallest details may not be productive to every game group, but y'know... We can TRY for basic decency.</div> </div> </div> </div> And to clarify, that would fit under the \u201cdon't be disrespectful\u201d bit that I think we all agree on. I am <i>not</i> saying that the fact that it's possible to go too far means that you shouldn't try at all; I'm just saying that there's a difference between \u201cdon't be disrespectful\u201d and \u201cgo for maximum respectfulness\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377108#post1377108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the original idea... At its core, it's going &quot;We know this culture existed but very little else so why not just make up a Pantheon?&quot; and my problem with that is... If you're going to make things up completely? To the point where you have no idea if there's even any tenuous connective tissue? <i>Why bother tying them to that culture</i>?<br /> <br /> Like, if you have information here and there, but have to use conjecture and supposition to fill in some blanks, then sure. But if all we have is a name of a God (and they may not even be a God because we don't have any additional context) so you're making up who they are, what they did, what their practices were, what relationships they have with other Possible Gods (half of whom you made up because we don't even have THOSE names in any records)... Like, if you're making up 99% of a Pantheon, you might as well just commit to your own original creation. I'm sure the original Gods that are being made up are absolutely fine, and heck, may even be great fun to read about.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that standard, we don't get the Gaulish Pantheon, as my understanding is that the vast majority of it is made up due to a near-complete lack of source material \u2014 and what we do have is filtered through the Romans' interpretation of the Gaulish Pantheon. <br /> <br /> And from what I recall, there's at least one developer who <i>likes</i> to work with largely unknown Pantheons because of the creative freedom that entails. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm <i>not</i> saying \u201cdon't even try to be respectful\u201d (a point that I'm belaboring because people seem to be jumping to the conclusion that that's exactly what I'm saying); I'm saying that it's possible to go too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T00:22:00-07:00","id":1377116,"title":"","content":"There actually is quite a lot of material available for the Nemetondevos! They have often been presented as this sort of height of a challenge due to lack of materials, but there is actually quite a lot through archeology and conjoined studies with Classical studies.<br /> <br /> The big issue is that the material that is available for them tends to be rather modern and academic. Such as the recent study that shows that Cernunnos most likely had nothing to do with animals or wilderness stuff but instead was a patron of merchants and wealth. So, totally a ton of material, could make a full like 'Pantheon' for them for sure as long as Underworld and Overworld being vague and uncertain is cool. <br /> <br /> I honestly was pretty sure the Nemetondevos were a lost cause until I did a bunch of research on my end. The resources are not at all easily accessible as they are all very recent innovations, but there's totally enough material to do a very good job with them! Totally a minimal amount of making stuff up is necessary. It is really heartwarming after having heard of them as an impossible task for the last decade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T00:32:09-07:00","id":1377119,"title":"","content":"Okay; I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T00:44:05-07:00","id":1377122,"title":"","content":"I'm really pleased to hear that about the Nemetondevos. I've always found them to be quite interesting, despite the scarcity of information, and I'm intrigued to see what you have to say about the official write-up when it comes out. I don't think a vague cosmology should be a problem. I'd probably handle it similarly to how the Tuatha De Danann were banished from their Overworld (i.e. Ireland), only having it be sealed away completely to the point that the gods themselves don't really remember it. Or just have it be vaguely defined in general, like the Enondeara's cosmology in their write-up. Also, Cernunnos is definitely a wealth deity in my games, and his current incarnation runs a mega-corp called Hart Industries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T06:48:52-07:00","id":1377166,"title":"","content":"Watcher, I didn't quote you but I gave you a like. I am always interested in things &quot;Celtic&quot; ( to the point I'm aware some English scholars dispute the value of that term). But my computer situation is messy. I'd love the PDFs Thank You!<br /> <br /> If you said you prefer the singular they, good for you.<br /> <br /> I snapped because I thought I was being scolded. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-29-2020, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T06:57:12-07:00","id":1377168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377110#post1377110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have the names of any gods by the way, we don't even know if they were polytheistic at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the only thing known about there faith is that a sailor reported that he was told their faith was neither Islam, Christianity, nor Buddhism. And that they were reported to have rituals. <br /> <br /> There seems to have been very little curiousity about these people when they existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T06:59:13-07:00","id":1377169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377116#post1377116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There actually is quite a lot of material available for the Nemetondevos! They have often been presented as this sort of height of a challenge due to lack of materials, but there is actually quite a lot through archeology and conjoined studies with Classical studies.<br /> <br /> The big issue is that the material that is available for them tends to be rather modern and academic. Such as the recent study that shows that Cernunnos most likely had nothing to do with animals or wilderness stuff but instead was a patron of merchants and wealth. So, totally a ton of material, could make a full like 'Pantheon' for them for sure as long as Underworld and Overworld being vague and uncertain is cool. <br /> <br /> I honestly was pretty sure the Nemetondevos were a lost cause until I did a bunch of research on my end. The resources are not at all easily accessible as they are all very recent innovations, but there's totally enough material to do a very good job with them! Totally a minimal amount of making stuff up is necessary. It is really heartwarming after having heard of them as an impossible task for the last decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T11:18:57-07:00","id":1377200,"title":"","content":"Why use a real culture when you can use Atlantis or any other similar one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T11:41:17-07:00","id":1377206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377200#post1377200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why use a real culture when you can use Atlantis or any other similar one.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do we know that Atlantis wasn't a real people that similarly got lost? For all we know, making stuff up about them is just as disrespectful as making stuff up about the culture that the original poster was referring to.<br /> <br /> No, I don't actually believe that Atlantis was real. I'm just making a point. just as it is possible to be insufficiently concerned about being disrespectful, it is also possible to be overly concerned about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-29-2020, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T11:55:54-07:00","id":1377207,"title":"","content":"Also, I took the original intent not as \u201clet's make up a new Pantheon and attach it to these lost people just because\u201d, but rather \u201clet's have a Pantheon that was worshipped by a loving culture until very recently \u2014 a Pantheon that had active supporters in the World that were contemporaries of the likes of the Aesir and the Kami until they got wiped out. Let's explore how this Pantheon reacts to the total loss of its mortal worshippers.\u201d<br /> <br /> That's the part of this idea that I like: it's kind of a flip side of the Nemontedavos, where the people survived (somewhat) but their gods were wiped out (assuming that they were, in 2e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T12:31:29-07:00","id":1377216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377207#post1377207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I took the original intent not as \u201clet's make up a new Pantheon and attach it to these lost people just because\u201d, but rather \u201clet's have a Pantheon that was worshipped by a loving culture until very recently \u2014 a Pantheon that had active supporters in the World that were contemporaries of the likes of the Aesir and the Kami until they got wiped out. Let's explore how this Pantheon reacts to the total loss of its mortal worshippers.\u201d<br /> <br /> That's the part of this idea that I like: it's kind of a flip side of the Nemontedavos, where the people survived (somewhat) but their gods were wiped out (assuming that they were, in 2e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that is the part I would like to concentrate on. We already covered the first part with the arguing. For the sake of arguing you don't even have to associate it with this specific lost culture, just say it was the exact same situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T12:48:44-07:00","id":1377218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377207#post1377207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I took the original intent not as \u201clet's make up a new Pantheon and attach it to these lost people just because\u201d, but rather \u201clet's have a Pantheon that was worshipped by a loving culture until very recently \u2014 a Pantheon that had active supporters in the World that were contemporaries of the likes of the Aesir and the Kami until they got wiped out. Let's explore how this Pantheon reacts to the total loss of its mortal worshippers.\u201d<br /> <br /> That's the part of this idea that I like: it's kind of a flip side of the Nemontedavos, where the people survived (somewhat) but their gods were wiped out (assuming that they were, in 2e).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you understood me. Thank You Dataweaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T14:34:20-07:00","id":1377226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1377206#post1377206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do we know that Atlantis wasn't a real people that similarly got lost? For all we know, making stuff up about them is just as disrespectful as making stuff up about the culture that the original poster was referring to..</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean we can be pretty sure that Atlantis didn't exist because when Plato proposed Atlantis he went &quot;Let's come up with a fake Utopia, let's call it Atlantis&quot;. Like that's the big thing that it seems got lost in a lot of Atlantis tellings. Atlantis was never really intended to be a literal place that literally existed, even when it was first proposed. It'd be like if I went &quot;Okay I'm going to make up a flying city, let's call it Zyphyeria, a very fictional city that is very deliberately not real&quot;<br /> <br /> And then thousands of years later a bunch of people went &quot;Zypheria existed, this mountain is the city where it crashed&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, no. No, Zypheria never existed. Any resemblance to any real-world culture was due to me being uncreative with designing Zypherian culture. Trying to claim that Zypheria ever existed or that I may be accidentally getting something wrong about a culture I know for certain does not exist is impossible. I'm not getting anything wrong about a culture that I, again, <i>made up and does not exist</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I don't actually believe that Atlantis was real. I'm just making a point. just as it is possible to be insufficiently concerned about being disrespectful, it is also possible to be overly concerned about it </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Being concerned with being respectful shows that you're trying and you give a shit. Being <i>dis</i>respectful is laughing in the faces of the people, alive or dead, who actually believed these things. If I had to pick one I'd rather be <i>too</i> polite. And 'It's just a game' is no excuse for being lazy and getting shit wrong.<br /> <br /> But on the original topic: A Pantheon whose people are wiped out can reforge their Legend in front of new Worshippers. If a Pantheon is slain while people who know of them exist, then people can claim the Mantles by emulating their Deeds.<br /> <br /> If a God is slain, and if all those who know this God are gone... If nobody can speak of this God's Deeds, and nobody can say who they are... If nobody can tell you who say, Thor is, and what Thor did, and what makes Thor Thor... <i>Did that God ever exist?</i><br /> <br /> So in the hypothetical scenario of &quot;Gods existed, their people are dead&quot;, it's possible for them to find new worshippers. Find them elsewhere. Worship doesn't actually give the Gods any power in Scion. They could demonstrate their power to other people and go &quot;I AM NYTRAX, LORD OF DREAMS&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T15:02:27-07:00","id":1377229,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest using Watcher and Sacerdos's write-up of the Zemis for the &quot;gods alive, worshippers dead,&quot; concept? That's more or less how they're depicted in the (very excellent and under-appreciated) write-up. They're an orphaned pantheon, and I would probably run them as being very interested in acquiring new worshippers, albeit worshippers who were not descended from the people involved in the genocide of the Taino. They're also very, very, interested in avenging their people as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T14:56:05-07:00","id":1377801,"title":"","content":"Also, looking into Mt. Tambora's location, I'd be very surprised if it weren't within the territory of the Hyangs, in regards to what the local pantheon would be. I'm pretty sure they're not the only pantheon in Indonesia, but it's right off the coast of their home base of Bali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:40:22-07:00","id":1377829,"title":"","content":"The Hyangs might have taken in the shellshocked pantheon, or tried to finish them off. Given how little we know about the locals, we don't even have a description of how folks said they looked, you can play that how you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:46:46-07:00","id":1377830,"title":"","content":"Looking around the nets archeologists seem to say the lost culture of Sumbawa had a papuan affinity. Well that's far more than they knew before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:55:36-07:00","id":1378383,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would also be reluctant to portray a pantheon or culture that was completely lost to us. If we have nothing to work with, we can't work with it, right?<br /> <br /> If you want to touch on a lost culture's pantheon, maybe you could explore what exactly that loss and the blank it leaves behind in the cultural landscape means to the rest of the gods. An entire real world culture just disappearing with no records of them is a sad and horrible thing and it should be sad and horrible in the World, as well. If a pantheon's cult is so completely destroyed that nothing - no names, no images, no one who remembers them - remains in the World, then perhaps they are just cut off from the World? Removed from existence by Fate? I would treat the potential Tamboran pantheon as exactly what the title of this thread calls them: a lost pantheon. They are not absent, dead, or temporarily disabled, they are just gone.<br /> <br /> So instead of asking how other pantheons would treat potential survivors, I think it might be interesting to think about how other pantheons would deal with seeing another group of gods just disappear. Just imagine the Hyang realising one morning in 1815 that their neighbour - a pantheon they have known for aeons - just vanished and they suddenly cannot remember a single thing about them. Were the gods of Tambora best friends, mortal enemies, casual acquaintances? Were they powerful, beautiful, terrible, or all of the above? Somehow the Hyang just can't remember.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:19:52-07:00","id":1378394,"title":"","content":"The only catch is that in Scion, gods don't depend on their mortal followers door their existence. If the culture that was mentioned in the first post worshipped a Pantheon that's distinct from the ones we know, those gods would <i>not</i> have been wiped out along with their followers. Gods not only <i>can</i> survive the destruction of their followers; it's not even particularly hard to do. And if anything, it would be exceptionally odd if they <i>didn't</i> survive the complete and utter destruction of their followers. <br /> <br /> So \u201chow do they react to another group of gods just disappearing?\u201d isn't what would happen either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:26:40-07:00","id":1378396,"title":"","content":"I think there is much fun and potential to be had in this sort of situation. I think history itself is often weirder then our imaginations sometimes and so using an actual point or moment or culture as the core for a campaign makes a lot of sense. Additionally, there can be quite a lot of fun in taking the bits and pieces we do know and filling in the gaps for your own campaign. <br /> <br /> This whole thing might not be something everyone would use at their gaming table but for those who find it intriguing, and I am one of them, I say thanks for posting it as it gives a gives me a good starting point for campaign development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T22:45:48-07:00","id":1378682,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong but the gods maintain human worshippers because it gives them a way to distinguish themselves from Titans allowing them to relate to humans and to define themselves and without those worshippers that distinction disappears<br /> So if a pantheons entire mortal culture was obliterated (or just stopped worshipping them as with Aten) but the gods still survived wouldn't they revert back into titans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24313-insert-original-name","name":"[Insert Original Name]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T00:41:34-07:00","id":1378691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[Insert Original Name]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1378682#post1378682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong but the gods maintain human worshippers because it gives them a way to distinguish themselves from Titans allowing them to relate to humans and to define themselves and without those worshippers that distinction disappears<br /> So if a pantheons entire mortal culture was obliterated (or just stopped worshipping them as with Aten) but the gods still survived wouldn't they revert back into titans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it necessarily reverts them to Titans. I don't feel like that's the right word at least. It would probably would start causing a sort of distancing from humanity and such with those who've most recently lost all their followers potentially looking for other options and ways to do thing with those who've lost their followers further back becoming more of an alien mindset closer to that of the titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T02:04:40-07:00","id":1378702,"title":"","content":"As far the rules are concerned, the great advantage of having worshipers is a stable source of legend in the forms of Fatebound and Sacrifices. Of course they must lend some of this legend to help the worshipers (otherwise they would just stop sacrificing things on the gods name, but often the gods can just keep the legend and do a minor trick to help them.<br /> <br /> The idea of becoming Titans is not bad, but I don\u2019t think a former human Scion would become a Titan for lack of worshipers. And there are Titan cults described somewhere (not sure if it\u2019s in 1e or 2e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T04:40:28-07:00","id":1378722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1376848-a-lost-pantheon?p=1378702#post1378702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far the rules are concerned, the great advantage of having worshipers is a stable source of legend in the forms of Fatebound and Sacrifices. Of course they must lend some of this legend to help the worshipers (otherwise they would just stop sacrificing things on the gods name, but often the gods can just keep the legend and do a minor trick to help them.<br /> <br /> The idea of becoming Titans is not bad, but I don\u2019t think a former human Scion would become a Titan for lack of worshipers. And there are Titan cults described somewhere (not sure if it\u2019s in 1e or 2e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Still it would give the pantheon in question motives to reconnect with the world. They might seek worshipers, or a mantel they could use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}